  "body": [
    "The premise is that the ground between buildings deserves the same investment as the buildings themselves. This district treats streets, drainage and shared infrastructure as the public work rather than as what is left over.",
    "The district is assembled from a catalogue rather than composed as a whole. Street and building modules, tilted at 0, 5, 10 and 15 degrees to suit the grade, establish a ground that carries its own drainage, utilities and stormwater basins. Blocks are then built against it, so the plan can extend or stop without redesign. Transit leads: the trolley runs level with the pavement, and private, public and pedestrian circulation are drawn as three separate networks.",
    "The ground pays for itself. Roofs collect energy, structure carries food production, and waste is processed on site at 700–900 degrees rather than hauled away. The shared rooms — library, gym, lecture hall and waterfront amphitheater — sit in the public fabric rather than behind an institution's door. Mapping the city's parks against municipal waste, and life expectancy against property value, set the targets."
  ],
